    "result_text": "Invoices that have a credit note against them now show a \"Credited\" badge next to their status in a project's invoice list. The acceptance test passes when run with `bin/e2e`.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Server:** each invoice in the project list now carries a `creditApplied` flag (`InvoiceResponse.java`). It's true when the credit notes against that invoice add up to more than zero. The list already added up each invoice's credits, so this adds no extra database queries.\n- **Front end:** `project-invoices.ts` shows the badge (`data-testid=\"invoice-credit-flag\"`) only on credited invoices. `invoice.service.ts` declares the new field, and `styles.css` gets a small outlined green style for the badge.\n- **Database:** I didn't add a migration. Credit notes already have their own table (`V53__create_credit_note.sql`), so the flag is worked out from that rather than stored separately.\n\nTwo differences from the request as written:\n- **Spring, not OfficeFloor:** the request mentions an OfficeFloor server, but this app is a Spring Boot app (as `CLAUDE.md` says), so I wrote it the Spring way.\n- **Where the badge appears:** only the project's invoice list. The all-invoices page and the client statement don't show it yet.",
